110_PW_DFPT_Si_X: Si fcc diamond, DFPT phonon at the X point.

Ground state: 2-atom fcc Si (a = 2 * 2.715 * 1.8897261255 = 10.2612
Bohr = 5.4300 Angstrom), ONCV PBE (Si_ONCV_PBE-1.0), 20/80 Ry,
4x4x4 Gamma-centered k-mesh, nbands=8.

DFPT: single q = (0, 0.5, 0.5) direct (fcc X point), 6 displacement
Sternheimer solves (v_sc_broyden default mixing), crystal ASR.

Note: the DFPT esolver is currently a serial implementation; MPI domain
decomposition is planned future work. Autotest.sh runs this case with a
single MPI rank regardless of the suite -n setting.

Expected frequencies (cm^-1): ~133.44 (TA), ~407.6 (LA), ~459.8 (LO).
Cross-validated against QE 6.8 (same pseudo, ecut, k-mesh): rms 0.17.

Tolerance: the per-case `threshold` file sets the comparison threshold
to 1e-4 for this case. Same-binary reruns reproduce the frequencies
exactly at the printed 6 decimals, so the margin only absorbs
last-digit rounding across compilers/toolchains.
